cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  vus-hindsight: a retrospective ClinVar VUS reclassification
  benchmark
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark or its measured counts, please cite
  the archived release rather than the repository URL — a
  repository link is not a stable reference, because re-running
  the pipeline against a newer ClinVar release legitimately
  changes the numbers.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Barra
    given-names: Gustavo Barcelos
    # Add your ORCID here once available:
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/gbbarra/vus-hindsight'
license: MIT
version: V1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-03'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21766106
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21766106
    description: >-
      Zenodo archive of this repository. Note that Zenodo mints both a
      concept DOI resolving to the newest version and a version DOI
      fixed to one release; when quoting specific counts, prefer the
      version DOI for V1.0.0 so the citation cannot drift onto a later
      release with different numbers.
abstract: >-
  Measures how many ClinVar variants of uncertain significance
  (VUS) were later reclassified to a definitive call, and sizes
  the pathogenic arm as material for evaluating variant
  interpretation methods. Version 1.0.0 is computed against the
  archived ClinVar monthly variant_summary_2026-07.txt.gz of
  2 July 2026; the md5 of every input file is recorded in
  results/transitions.md so the counts are re-derivable rather
  than merely re-runnable. The endpoint is deliberately an
  archived monthly rather than the rolling variant_summary.txt.gz,
  which NCBI overwrites in place and which therefore cannot be
  reproduced once superseded.
keywords:
  - ClinVar
  - variant of uncertain significance
  - variant reclassification
  - variant interpretation
  - benchmark
  - clinical genetics
